In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to them as
both strict obligations and conditions to all your licenses.

2.  Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software to do
everything you might do with the software that would otherwise infringe the
licensor's copyright in it for any permitted purpose. However, you may
only distribute the software according to Distribution and you may only
make changes according to Changes and New Works.

3.  Distribution

You may distribute copies of the software to others, but only if:

- you do not charge any fee for the software;
- you do not use the software for any commercial purpose;
- you keep intact all copyright and other notices, including this license;
- you give each recipient a copy of this license;
- you provide each recipient with a copy of the source code, or a way to get
  a copy of the source code.

4.  Changes and New Works

You may make changes to the software, or create new works from it, and
distribute them, but only if:

- you do not charge any fee for the software;
- you do not use the software for any commercial purpose;
- you keep intact all copyright and other notices, including this license;
- you give each recipient a copy of this license;
- you provide each recipient with a copy of the source code, or a way to get
  a copy of the source code;
- you clearly mark any changes you make, or new works you create, as
  different from the original software;
- you do not use the licensor's name, trademarks, or service marks to
  endorse or promote the new work, or in any other way, without the
  licensor's prior written permission.

5.  Patents

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software to do everything
with the software that would otherwise infringe any patent claims the
